  "talks": [
    {
      "slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "title": "I Run a Fleet of AI Agents Across Three Machines. Here's What Broke.",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ",
      "track": "",
      "day": null,
      "room": null,
      "is_sole_speaker": true
    }
  ],
  "sessions": [],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "At that point, I'm not running agents anymore. I've become the scheduler, deciding who does what.",
      "timestamp_sec": 35,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=35s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "I just couldn't hold what six agents were doing at once. My own attention was the bottleneck.",
      "timestamp_sec": 73,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=73s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "How does a handful of executives run a company of thousands of people? They don't hold all of it in their heads. They separate context. Each person only ever sees their own slice.",
      "timestamp_sec": 73,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=73s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "These are real entity types in the system. It is not a cute metaphor. Each one is its own agent with its own scoped context and its own approval boundary.",
      "timestamp_sec": 111,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=111s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So, instead of holding six contexts in my head, I hold exactly one.",
      "timestamp_sec": 111,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=111s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "The state lives in files. It is not trapped inside one model. And this is the single most practical thing I learned all year.",
      "timestamp_sec": 145,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=145s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "I stopped doing it. It's slow. I can't choose what survives. And whatever it throws away is just gone.",
      "timestamp_sec": 145,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=145s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So, instead, I don't compact, I reset. And by reset, I mean right inside Claude, I clear the context completely.",
      "timestamp_sec": 145,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=145s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "The context can get wiped, the machine can even crash, and the work still survives because it was never only in the model.",
      "timestamp_sec": 190,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=190s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Any layer that wants to act submits its plan and then it blocks. It waits. Nothing runs until I approve.",
      "timestamp_sec": 190,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=190s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So I forced its hand. A CLI harness with skills that call those CLIs. So dispatching becomes the only path it can take.",
      "timestamp_sec": 228,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=228s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "And honestly, I didn't build this gateway by hand. An infra team inside the fleet built it. Agents building the tools that run the agents.",
      "timestamp_sec": 228,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=228s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "The expectation is clean. Credential A to workspace A, credential B to workspace B, one to one. The reality, they collided, crossed over, bound to the wrong workspaces.",
      "timestamp_sec": 307,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=307s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So, the very first thing I did was build a boot command, one overlord boot, and the whole fleet comes straight back up because all the state was sitting in files.",
      "timestamp_sec": 307,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=307s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Per-machine directories for machine-specific state, and the shared stuff only changes through a pull request. It's boring, but boring is what stops the two machines from silently disagreeing.",
      "timestamp_sec": 394,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=394s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Your one point of control can't be a thing that falls asleep.",
      "timestamp_sec": 430,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=430s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "at one point I went looking for a feature I'd built, and I genuinely could not remember which machine I'd built it on",
      "timestamp_sec": 430,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=430s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "An agent should just declare what it needs, not where it runs.",
      "timestamp_sec": 465,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=465s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "These are the exact questions Kubernetes already answers. So, that's where I'm headed. I'm not going to reinvent compute, secrets, and tools. Kubernetes already nailed those.",
      "timestamp_sec": 503,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=503s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "One machine, I solved. Across machines, still rough, still building.",
      "timestamp_sec": 503,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=503s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    }
  ],
  "positions": [
    {
      "claim": "A flat pile of parallel agents does not scale because the human is forced into three roles at once — scheduler, memory, and reviewer.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 73,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=73s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Agent hierarchies should be implemented as real entity types with scoped context and approval boundaries, not used as a descriptive metaphor.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 111,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=111s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Context compaction is the wrong default: it is slow, gives you no control over what survives, and permanently discards what it drops.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 145,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=145s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Clearing context entirely and re-reading self-written handoff and history files is a better recovery mechanism than summarizing history.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 145,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=145s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Agent state kept in files on disk survives context wipes and machine crashes, whereas state in the model's context window does not.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 190,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=190s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Orchestrator agents will do the work themselves instead of delegating unless the tooling makes dispatching the only available path.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 269,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=269s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Stacked Claude Code and MCP processes on a single machine will exhaust memory and fill swap.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 307,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=307s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Two machines pointing at the same shared context directory will produce conflicts and silent divergence unless machine-specific state is separated and shared state is changed only via pull request.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 394,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=394s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "The fleet's single control point must run on an always-on machine, because a laptop that sleeps cannot serve as a control plane.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 430,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYl2_mqmnQ&t=430s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Agents should declare their resource requirements rather than having a human decide which machine they run on.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 465,
      "talk_slug": "i-run-a-fleet-of-ai-agents-across-three-machines-heres-what-broke",
